  "tagline": "Classic C DBM library from FAL Labs; unmaintained since 2012 and twice superseded.",
  "description": "Tokyo Cabinet was a fast C library implementing hash, B+tree, fixed-length and table (schemaless record) databases, and with its companion network server Tokyo Tyrant it was one of the original 'NoSQL' darlings around 2008-2010, used notably at mixi. Its author moved on to Kyoto Cabinet and later Tkrzw, and the final release, 1.4.48, dates from August 2012. FAL Labs' page itself recommends Tkrzw. It should be considered discontinued.",
